        <mxCell id="header-sub" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#e2e8f0&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;What is the AI gateway made of, and what happens inside it between an agent&amp;#39;s request and the model&amp;#39;s answer?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;Scope: agentgateway on its own GatewayClass, beside Envoy Gateway, on-prem K3s · drawn in full: what the proposal adds (IA-1, guardrails, MCP and A2A in IA-2) · faded: what already runs&lt;br&gt;Out of scope: Vault and the secrets operator (zoom 6) · OPA through extAuth (IA-3) · the Envoy Gateway that serves apps and users · the same gateway on EKS and GKE&lt;br&gt;Assumed: Gemini through several keys in the first priority group, the GPU server in the second; one proxy replica. Resource names come from agentgateway.dev/docs/kubernetes/latest; the phase 1 trial confirms them&lt;br&gt;v0.2 · source: cnp-docs/architecture/cnp · agentgateway docs (architecture, policy order, LLM, MCP, A2A)&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#94a3b8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
